          "short": "Club 1 has a wider spread of ages, from 11 to 82 years, compared with 37 to 73 years for Club 2. Club 1 has eight members in their seventies and two aged 82; Club 2 has most members in their sixties and five in their seventies.",
          "worked": "Club 1 includes teenagers and members in their twenties, whereas Club 2’s youngest member is 37. The age ranges are $82-11=71$ years for Club 1 and $73-37=36$ years for Club 2, so Club 1 has a wider spread. Club 1 has eight members in their seventies and two aged 82. Club 2 has nine members in their sixties, its largest age group, and five in their seventies.",
